  "id": "DrugBank_DB00515 - MONDO_18172",
  "verbalization": "Cisplatin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary through a series of indirect pathways involving other entities. The evidence suggests that Cisplatin may act as a mediator in the development of this tumor, as it is linked to Immature Ovarian Teratoma and Melphalan, both of which are associated with the same target disease. The presence of Cisplatin in the indication chain for Immature Ovarian Teratoma and its subsequent link to Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary implies a potential role in tumor progression or maintenance. Similarly, the connection between Cisplatin and Familial Ovarian Cancer, which in turn links to Tretamine and the target tumor, further supports a broader biological pathway involving chemotherapy agents. The integration of these pathways suggests that Cisplatin may influence the tumor's biology through mechanisms that are not yet fully understood, potentially involving chemotherapy-induced cellular changes or tumor-specific signaling pathways. The evidence is consistent with a role for Cisplatin in the development or progression of this tumor, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
